      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right; trying to force a foundation that has crumbled to stand is just a recipe for more pain, and that exhaustion is valid. It isn't a failure of your will to rebuild, but rather a sign that the current structure is fundamentally unsustainable, and that is not your fault. Sometimes the only way to truly heal is to let go of the broken parts entirely and start from nothing, even if that feels terrifying.",
      "source": "target",
